1. DEFINITIONS

"Licensor" means the copyright holder named above.

"Software" means the work, in source code and object code, together with
its documentation, that the Licensor makes available under this License.

"Modification" means any change to, addition to, or deletion from the
files of the Software, and any new file that contains a substantial
portion of the Software's code. A work that merely uses the Software
through its interfaces — including by linking to it, embedding it, or
defining host function bindings (such as extern functions) for it — is
not a Modification, but such a work remains subject to Section 3. A
separate work that explains, quotes, or teaches the Software is not a
Modification.

"Program" means source code, a template, a script, or a spec written in
the Acvus language, or in any other language whose programs the
Software parses, checks, compiles, or executes, including a language
whose front end lowers its programs to the intermediate representation
of the Software or of any language the Software embeds. "A language
built on the Software" means such a language, other than the Acvus
language itself.

"Value" means data that carries no computation of its own: numbers,
booleans, characters, text, bytes, arrays, tuples, objects, and variants
of these, and values of types a host defines that hold only such data.
A Value contains no expression, function, or statement. It remains a
Value when the Software type-checks it, rejects it, stores it, or embeds
it as a constant in a Program. Text is a Value unless it is itself
parsed as a Program.

"User Content" means Programs and Values, other than those included in
the Software, together with the output the Software produces from them.

"Language Product" and "Sell" have the meanings given in Section 3.


